    "slug": "stacks",
    "title": "AI-First Development with Stacks",
    "excerpt": "Stacks is a new way to share AI project templates on Nostr. Browse starter kits, remix your own, and deploy lightning-fast AI apps — all from the terminal.",
    "coverImage": "/assets/images/stacks.png",
    "date": "2025-05-10",
    "author": {},
    "ogImage": {},
    "content": "## Stacks: AI-First Development\n\n**[Stacks](https://getstacks.dev) is a decentralized template-sharing platform built on [Nostr](/blog/nostr101/), designed specifically to jumpstart AI development.**\n\n- Publish AI-first project templates (called \"stacks\")\n- Quickly bootstrap working apps from these templates\n- Deploy functional applications in minutes\n\nStacks are shared via Nostr events, meaning they’re portable, censorship-resistant, and social. A stack can be anything from a [simple website template](https://getstacks.dev/stack/naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzppscgyy746fhmrt0nq955z6xmf80pkvrat0yq0hpknqtd00z8z68qqrk6ennw3skx6c04w4fd) to a [AI chat app](https://getstacks.dev/stack/naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqq9kz6fdvd5xzapdvdkxjcz8fx7), or even a [GameBoy ROM](https://getstacks.dev/stack/naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqqpxwcsx699p0)!\n\n  Explore stacks at [getstacks.dev](https://getstacks.dev)\n\n  [Try AI-first building with Stacks!](https://getstacks.dev)\n\n---\n\n## How to Use Stacks\n\nInstall stacks CLI:\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g @getstacks/stacks\n```\n\nOnce installed, you can add stacks and start building. \n\n  Installing the [pg-relay stack](https://getstacks.dev/stack/naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqqy8qeedwfjkcctehjfz9x)\n\nFor example, if you want to build a Nostr Relay, you can add the `pg-relay` stack:\n\n```bash\nstacks add naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqqy8qeedwfjkcctehjfz9x\n```\n\nThis will add the stack to your local collection. You can view all the stacks you have added and their aliases with:\n\n```bash\nstacks list\n\nStack Aliases (2):\n---------------------\nmkstack => nostr:naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqqrk66mnw3skx6c4g6ltw\npg-relay => nostr:naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqqy8qeedwfjkcctehjfz9x\n\n```\n\nRunning the stack will create a project in your current directory:\n\n```bash\nstacks pg-relay\n```\nFrom there, you can prompt our built-in AI Agent \"Dork\" to help you build your app! Dork similar to [Goose](https://getgoose.ai), but fine-tuned to specialize in building with stacks. Dork helps generate boilerplate code, answer questions about your dependencies, and guide you through deployments. \n\n> **Open Router API:** Open Router API Key is currently required to get the most out of building stacks. You can sign up and get one here: [https://openrouter.ai](https://openrouter.ai). In the future we hope to offer a service to accept zaps to run the AI for users who don't wish to directly pay for Open Router. \n\n---\n\n## Try Building a Nostr App with MKStack\n\n  [View Video](https://www.youtube.com/embed/kJRwAGmAmGI)\n\nWant to see Stacks in action? Check out [MKstack](https://getstacks.dev/stack/naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqqrk66mnw3skx6c4g6ltw), a Nostr template built using:\n\n- [Nostrbook MCP](/blog/nostrbook-mcp) for queryable documentation\n- Built-in Nostr login\n- Context files to supercharge AI workflows\n\nAdd MKStack and run it:\n\n```bash\nstacks add naddr1qvzqqqrhl5pzqprpljlvcnpnw3pejvkkhrc3y6wvmd7vjuad0fg2ud3dky66gaxaqqrk66mnw3skx6c4g6ltw\n\nstacks mkstack\n```\nThen give Dork a prompt to get started. For example:\n\n```bash\n➜  stacks mkstack \n│\n◇  Enter project name\n│  nostr-chat-app\n│\n◇  \n│\n◆  CONTEXT.md found\n│\n◇   Dork here! I'm ready to help you with nostr-chat-app. What do you need?\n│  Please build a NIP-28 group chat add with Nostr login\n\n```\n\nDork will then use the [Nostrbook MCP](/_blog/nostrbook-mcp.mdx) to find the best way to build your app, pulling in the template components as needed.\n\nWhen it's finished, you can run the app with:\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n``` \n\nIf you like what you see, deploy it with the built-in Surge integration:\n\n```bash\nnpm run deploy\n```\n\nSee example of a site built and deployed this way here: [http://nip28.surge.sh/](http://nip28.surge.sh/)\n\n  Build a Nostr chat app with MKStack\n\n> **Note:** Surge is a free static hosting service that allows you to deploy your app with a single command. You will need to set up a free account on Surge if you want to deply this way: [https://surge.sh](https://surge.sh)\n\nYou have now deployed a fully functioning Nostr Chat app in only a few commands - and NO code written! \n\n---\n\n## Publish Your Own with the Stacks Protocol\n\nThe [Stacks Protocol](https://getstacks.dev/docs/protocol) defines how project templates and AI agents are structured, shared, and consumed. It consists of several key components:\n\n- stack.json - Metadata for project templates\n- agent.json - Configuration for AI agents\n- CONTEXT.md - Project context for AI agents\n- Nostr Integration - Decentralized publishing and discovery\n\nStack templates are published as Nostr events with kind `30717`. The stacks publish command converts the stack.json file into this Nostr event format and then publishes it. Each published stack has a unique identifier starting with naddr1, which encodes the event information in a compact format. This naddr1 is then used with the Stacks CLI to clone the stack or create an alias.\n\n[Publish your own stack →](https://getstacks.dev/publish)\n\n---\n\n## Try Our Other Tools for the Best Nostr Development Experience\n\nStacks is just one part of a growing toolkit designed to make building on Nostr easier and more powerful. Check out our other tools:\n\n- **Nostrify** – Bring your projects to life on Nostr with simple tools for relays, storage, signers, moderation policies, and more. [Try Nostrify →](https://nostrify.dev/)\n- **Nostrbook MCP** – A Comprehensive Registry of Nostr Documentation. Structured, detailed knowledge about Nostr for both humans and AI. [Try Nostrbook →](https://nostrbook.dev/)\n\n### Get notified of new releases!\n\n  [Explore Nostr Development Tools](https://soapbox.pub/tools/)\n\n---"
